# Fly Python dependencies — high-level spec (human-edited).
#
# This is the INPUT to pip-compile. The fully-pinned lock file
# requirements_lock.txt is generated from it and is what bazel's pip.parse
# consumes (see MODULE.bazel). Edit this file, then regenerate the lock:
#
#     pip-compile --resolver=backtracking requirements.in
#
# The C++/bazel build is self-contained (eigen, googletest, nanobind, bitsery
# are pinned in MODULE.bazel). The packages below are the Python third-party
# deps imported by production code (src/) and QA tests (qa/). Before this file
# existed, they were resolved from the system site-packages implicitly, which
# broke on any machine without them installed (QA 44-test failure root cause).

# cloudpickle — user-script task serialization (src/task/py/task.py,
#   src/agent/py/executor.py, src/fly/mapreduce.py). Without it production
#   code falls back to stdlib pickle, which cannot pickle lambdas / nested
#   functions under __main__, breaking user-script tasks and mapreduce.
cloudpickle>=3.0

# numpy / scipy — distributed RAS solver (src/solver/py/ras_graph.py uses
#   scipy.sparse + splu). Only stable APIs; no version-sensitive features.
numpy>=1.26
scipy>=1.11

# pytest — Python unit test runner (some src/**/tests/test_*.py cases).
pytest>=7.0

# coverage.py — 测量基础设施（2026-09-02）：覆盖率专项把 bazel py_test 纳入
# 采集（tools/measure_coverage.sh），sitecustomize 在 py_test 进程内自启
# coverage 需要本包在 bazel pip hub 中（hermetic 工具链不含系统 site-packages）。
coverage>=7.6
